<title>UK: Partners leaps to premium on LSE debut.</title>
<headline>Partners leaps to premium on LSE debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in stationery retailer Partners Holdings Plc leapt to a premium on Monday in the their first day of dealings on the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Partners' shares, issued at 150p, jumped to 169-1/2p by 1129 GMT in volume of 868,195 shares.</p>
<p>The company raised 5.05 million stg, after expenses, through a placing valuing it at 28 million stg.</p>
<p>Partners said it plans to increase its store portfolio from 80 stores to 220 by the year 2001 and forecast pre-tax profits of two million stg for the year to March 31 1997, against 1.15 million for the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
